## Heuristics

- An empty diff means no operator change; treat as unintentional unless the
  diagnosis itself reports a deliberate trigger.
- A diff that only touches paths inside the deterministic-repair allowlist
  (timeouts, retry knobs, max tokens, prompt template selection, tool parser)
  is *probably* operator-driven if the new value is plausible — call it
  intentional with medium confidence.
- A diff that touches ``model_providers.<id>.model.endpoint.base_url`` or
  ``active_model_provider`` is almost always operator-driven — intentional.
- A diff outside the recipe allowlist (random keys, hardware fields, version)
  is suspicious — call it unintentional or uncertain.
- If recent activity shows the same recipe failing repeatedly without a config
  diff, prefer ``ask_human``.

